stream
BT /F1 11 Tf 15 TL 56 732 Td
(Network Services Service Level Agreement - Standard Plan) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(1. Availability) Tj T*
(The minimum uptime requirement for network services on the Standard plan is 99.9%,) Tj T*
(measured on a monthly basis. Uptime is calculated as the total minutes in the month) Tj T*
(minus minutes of unplanned downtime, divided by the total minutes in the month.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(2. Performance Targets) Tj T*
(Round-trip latency within a single region must stay below 50 milliseconds. Packet loss) Tj T*
(must stay below 0.1% averaged over the month.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(3. Scheduled Maintenance) Tj T*
(Planned maintenance takes place every Sunday between 02:00 and 04:00 UTC. Customers) Tj T*
(receive at least 72 hours of notice before any maintenance window. Time spent in) Tj T*
(announced maintenance windows does not count as downtime.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(4. Incident Response Times \(Standard Plan\)) Tj T*
(Critical incidents receive a first response within 1 hour. High priority incidents) Tj T*
(receive a first response within 4 hours. Normal priority incidents receive a first) Tj T*
(response within 1 business day.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(5. Service Credits) Tj T*
(If monthly uptime falls below 99.9% but is at least 99.0%, the customer receives a) Tj T*
(service credit of 10% of that month's network fees. If monthly uptime falls below 99.0%,) Tj T*
(the customer receives a service credit of 25% of that month's network fees. Credits must) Tj T*
(be claimed within 30 days of the end of the affected month by opening a billing ticket.) Tj T*
(Credits are applied to the next invoice and are not paid out in cash.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(6. Exclusions) Tj T*
(Downtime caused by force majeure events, by the customer's own equipment or) Tj T*
(configuration changes, or by third-party services outside our network is excluded from) Tj T*
(uptime calculations.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
